# 10am late-start nudge (CFO directive 2026-09-10: "these late starters who are
# clocking in after 8.15am, by 10am send them just a reminder you started late
# today"). The command shipped in PR #829 on 10-Sep but was never scheduled, so
# not a single nudge went out — found 11-Sep when the CFO asked whether it had.
#
# Reads today's Time Doctor worklog, finds first activity after 08:15, and sends
# each person a short private reminder. It NEVER docks pay and it never copies a
# manager — the naming already happens in the daily workforce email. Excluded:
# the C-suite, anyone on approved leave, and anyone carrying a
# TrackingDirective(expected_to_track=False).
#
# 10:00 SAST = 08:00 UTC, Mon-Fri. This sits after the 09:40/09:45 intraday pull
# in hours-reminders.cron only on paper — that pull is later in the day, so this
# job reads the worklog live from Time Doctor itself.
#
# Runs through /usr/local/bin/omni-manage, which waits out a blue/green deploy
# window instead of failing with "backend is not running". Clock is UTC.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

0 8 * * 1-5 root cd /opt/alpha-finance && /usr/local/bin/omni-manage send_late_reminder --send >> /var/log/alpha-finance/late-reminder.log 2>&1
